\subsection{Research Question 2: Evaluating Model Performance}
\label{sec:RS2}

In this section, we evaluate and compare the performance of the three classification methods used to predict employment status: K-nearest neighbors(KNN), the pruned classification tree selected under the 1-SE rule, and the support vector machine with the polynomial degree 2 kernel, each identified as the best-performing within its own method in section(Section~\ref{sec:RS1}). For each model, we computed a confusion matrix, a precision-recall curve (PR), and a receiver operating characteristic curve (ROC), placing more weight and importance on the PR curve than on the ROC curve, as discussed earlier. 

